# Copy to .env for local work. docker compose up -d starts the database
# these credentials belong to; they are local-only and not secret.
# pnpm test:db REFUSES this database (R877): its files empty tables, so it runs only on a monreleve_* scratch one - see README.md.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://frontalier:frontalier@localhost:5436/frontalier?schema=public"

# FW14: the alert list. Unset means confirmation emails are collected in
# memory and never delivered - correct for tests and development. See
# lib/alerts/mailer.ts and the FW28 note in tasks/todo.md.
RESEND_API_KEY=""

# FW25: signs the short-lived token that lets /releve/print render one year.
#
# THE PRINT ROUTE REFUSES THIS PLACEHOLDER BY VALUE, not by hoping nobody
# deploys it - lib/export/print-token.ts compares against it explicitly and
# answers `not_configured`. A signing key everybody has is not a signing key.
#
# Generate a real one with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
AUTH_SECRET=change-me-local-only-not-for-deployment

# FW27: Firebase Cloud Messaging, for the daily reminder push.
#
# UNSET IS THE EXPECTED STATE TODAY. There is no Firebase project - R243
# forbids this task from seeking one. With no credentials `pnpm dev` PRINTS
# each reminder to the terminal and delivers nothing, and production refuses to
# schedule the reminder job at all rather than reporting sends that reached no
# device. See lib/push/resolve.ts for why a silent success is worse here than
# a refusal, and the opposite of the mailer's answer one surface over.
#
# THE PLACEHOLDERS BELOW ARE REFUSED BY VALUE, like AUTH_SECRET above:
# lib/push/fcm.ts compares against them and answers `placeholder_credentials`,
# which is a DIFFERENT refusal from `not_configured` because the two send
# whoever is debugging to different places.
#
# FCM_PRIVATE_KEY is the service account JSON's `private_key` with its
# newlines escaped as \n - which is how a .env file, a Coolify variable and a
# CI secret can each hold it on one line.
FCM_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id
FCM_CLIENT_EMAIL=service-account@your-firebase-project-id.iam.gserviceaccount.com
FCM_PRIVATE_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_THE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY
